NEARS-3646 QA — Photo step has no client-side size/type validation, so AC-LOG's own listed
failure path ("photo upload failing (size/type rejected, network)") has no way to be reached for
the size/type half.

Code (UserApp/lib/features/auth/controllers/deliveryman_registration_controller.dart:128-143,
pickIdentityFrontImage/pickIdentityBackImage similarly at line ~464):

  void pickDmImage(bool isLogo, bool isRemove) async {
    if (isRemove) { ... } else {
      if (isLogo) {
        _pickedImage = await ImagePicker().pickImage(source: ImageSource.gallery);
      } else {
        XFile? xFile = await ImagePicker().pickImage(source: ImageSource.gallery);
        if (xFile != null) { _pickedIdentities.add(xFile); }
      }
      update();
    }
  }

No file-size check, no MIME/extension check, anywhere in the pick path — whatever
ImagePicker().pickImage() returns is accepted unconditionally and forwarded to the multipart
submit. The visible hint text ("JPG, JPEG, PNG Less Than 1MB (Ratio 1:1)" / dp_photo_hint) is
purely decorative copy; nothing enforces it client-side, and there is no corresponding
AppLogger.warn/error call for a rejected file because no rejection ever happens on this path.

The only way a real "photo upload failure" can occur is a NETWORK/SERVER failure at final
submit time (already covered by the separate, already-logged
'delivery_partner_registration_submit_failed' path) — the size/type half of the AC-LOG line is,
as shipped, unreachable.

Severity: Medium — AC-LOG names this failure path explicitly; as built it can only ever be
exercised for the network half, never the size/type half.
